01:01:54.024 --> 01:01:56.313
- That's like the concept
of money essentially,

01:01:56.313 --> 01:01:57.695
'cause like some people who have like,

01:01:57.695 --> 01:02:00.585
they'd have like 1,000 bucks
in that entire savings.

01:02:00.585 --> 01:02:01.418
Some people would blow
that all in gift giving.

01:02:01.418 --> 01:02:02.251
- All right.

01:02:03.207 --> 01:02:05.785
'Cause that's how much it means to them.

01:02:05.785 --> 01:02:06.810
It's like money doesn't
mean anything if its a gift.

01:02:06.810 --> 01:02:08.819
- And not to like undermine
people like that, of course,

01:02:08.819 --> 01:02:10.734
but you know, like weirdly..

01:02:10.734 --> 01:02:13.758
Yeah, I completely get what
Garnt says where it's like...

01:02:13.758 --> 01:02:17.000
Especially when it's during
a time, like Christmas

01:02:17.000 --> 01:02:19.137
where you're giving each other gifts,

01:02:19.137 --> 01:02:19.970
if I received something
really expensive from like,

01:02:19.970 --> 01:02:20.803
you know a parent or something right,

01:02:20.803 --> 01:02:21.636
then I would feel really bad,

01:02:25.848 --> 01:02:28.378
being like, oh man, you spent
so much money on this gift

01:02:28.378 --> 01:02:29.211
while I gave you a bottle of wine.

01:02:29.211 --> 01:02:30.044
(Garnt laughs)

01:02:31.571 --> 01:02:33.774
- What if that was a $10,000
bottle of wine, Joey come on?

01:02:33.774 --> 01:02:34.607
- Yeah, but what if it
was like a $20 bottle

01:02:34.607 --> 01:02:35.440
of wine, you know?

01:02:35.440 --> 01:02:36.441
- (Connor mumbles)

01:02:36.441 --> 01:02:37.274
- Unless the disparicy, what disparity

01:02:43.430 --> 01:02:44.263
- Yeah, disparity.

01:02:44.263 --> 01:02:45.096
- Oh my God, the spelling
again, the disparity.

01:02:46.989 --> 01:02:47.822
Unless the disparity is like a lot,

01:02:47.822 --> 01:02:48.655
I don't think it matters.

01:02:50.899 --> 01:02:52.491
If you buy something for 50 bucks

01:02:52.491 --> 01:02:55.916
and they buy something
for 150, get over it.

01:02:55.916 --> 01:02:56.749
- Yeah I mean, that
doesn't matter too much

01:02:56.749 --> 01:02:57.582
but I mean as a uni student,

01:02:59.922 --> 01:03:01.696
I remember that was like.

01:03:01.696 --> 01:03:03.039
- That was like nine days.

01:03:03.039 --> 01:03:05.823
- But in university, at least what we did,

01:03:05.823 --> 01:03:07.931
'cause we were all broke,
we agreed on a price.

01:03:07.931 --> 01:03:08.874
Like you wouldn't spend
anything above that.

01:03:08.874 --> 01:03:09.707
- I like that, if you agree on a price,

01:03:09.707 --> 01:03:10.540
I like having systems in place.

01:03:12.999 --> 01:03:16.422
What scares me the most is just no rules,

01:03:16.422 --> 01:03:17.452
everywhere, it's a fucking free throw.

01:03:17.452 --> 01:03:19.440
- Well, with Sydney or Aki,

01:03:19.440 --> 01:03:21.652
do you agree on how much
you're spending on each other?

01:03:21.652 --> 01:03:23.326
- No.
- You just kinda like...

01:03:23.326 --> 01:03:24.472
So Sydney could spend 200

01:03:24.472 --> 01:03:27.581
and you could spend like a grand on her?

01:03:27.581 --> 01:03:28.414
- I guess yeah, like theoretically.

01:03:28.414 --> 01:03:29.651
- Theoretically.

01:03:29.651 --> 01:03:31.269
- Have there ever been
in something like that

01:03:31.269 --> 01:03:33.838
where there's been a big
gap in perceived value.

01:03:33.838 --> 01:03:36.156
- No because, I don't
think we tell each other

01:03:36.156 --> 01:03:37.336
how much it was.

01:03:37.336 --> 01:03:38.851
- I Mean, there's--

01:03:38.851 --> 01:03:40.523
- I know when there's Air Max Jordans.

01:03:40.523 --> 01:03:41.356
I know how much that
were when they pop in.

01:03:41.356 --> 01:03:42.690
(Garnt laughs)

01:03:42.690 --> 01:03:44.034
- Yeah, I don't know, man.

01:03:44.034 --> 01:03:46.243
How would you feel if I got
you a gift and I was like,

01:03:46.243 --> 01:03:47.919
you know how expensive
that shoe was, darling?

01:03:47.919 --> 01:03:50.983
- No, is like, if I knew
the value of the thing.

01:03:50.983 --> 01:03:51.883
- Oh, yeah.
- Yeah.

01:03:51.883 --> 01:03:55.305
- If it's something that I
obviously follow, I would know.

01:03:55.305 --> 01:03:58.307
And then you would know what you paid.

01:03:58.307 --> 01:04:00.984
- For me and Sydney,
it's different I guess

01:04:00.984 --> 01:04:03.310
because I know Sydney.

01:04:03.310 --> 01:04:05.548
- Well, that's why I'm asking.

01:04:05.548 --> 01:04:10.180
- I feel like I can communicate
with Sydney subconsciously,

01:04:10.180 --> 01:04:12.689
we know, we've been with each other for--

01:04:12.689 --> 01:04:15.554
- There've never been an
issue with gift-giving,

01:04:15.554 --> 01:04:17.782
that one of you just
bought more than the other?

01:04:17.782 --> 01:04:18.615
- No.

01:04:18.615 --> 01:04:21.335
- Aki and I buy each other
gifts all the time, though.

01:04:21.335 --> 01:04:23.205
So it's not really an issue

01:04:23.205 --> 01:04:25.832
when it comes to birthdays
or Christmas or anything.

01:04:25.832 --> 01:04:27.038
- For me, it's just...

01:04:27.038 --> 01:04:29.578
Another thing is as well as, is that

01:04:29.578 --> 01:04:31.652
I think I just suck at shopping.

01:04:31.652 --> 01:04:35.902
If shopping was a ranked
game, I'd be bronze level.

01:04:36.943 --> 01:04:37.776
No, I'd be fucking iron man.

01:04:37.776 --> 01:04:38.609
Like me and shopping--

01:04:40.207 --> 01:04:43.046
- I wouldn't be rock, I
would just be a stone.

01:04:43.046 --> 01:04:47.463
- Gift giving aside me and
shopping is when I shop,

01:04:49.237 --> 01:04:50.740
I know exactly what I want.

01:04:50.740 --> 01:04:53.719
And if I don't know what I
want, I'm so fucking lost.

01:04:53.719 --> 01:04:55.741
I go into a store and I'm just like.

01:04:55.741 --> 01:04:57.412
- I try really fucking hard,

01:04:57.412 --> 01:05:01.335
'cause I'm so bad at knowing
what my friends want.

01:05:01.335 --> 01:05:03.105
And that's why I struggled a lot

01:05:03.105 --> 01:05:06.416
but I just spend a lot
of time just thinking,

01:05:06.416 --> 01:05:08.525
like, all right, well, Garnt mention this,

01:05:08.525 --> 01:05:11.417
okay, well, yeah, Garnt kinda into this.

01:05:11.417 --> 01:05:13.823
So I kinda like run
through things in my head.

01:05:13.823 --> 01:05:14.858
I'm like, I gonna buy you something

01:05:14.858 --> 01:05:16.579
that you would never buy for yourself,

01:05:16.579 --> 01:05:18.263
that you would someone else buying.

01:05:18.263 --> 01:05:20.175
Just how I do gifts.

01:05:20.175 --> 01:05:22.539
- Meanwhile for me, it's
like, I have to stop myself

01:05:22.539 --> 01:05:23.372
from texting Garnt and
saying, "What do you want?"

01:05:23.372 --> 01:05:24.205
(Garnt laughs)

01:05:26.572 --> 01:05:27.405
"What do you want for your
birthday?" I don't know.

01:05:27.405 --> 01:05:29.772
- I'm also not against that,
if someone wants to ask me,

01:05:29.772 --> 01:05:31.551
if someone is like,
Connor, what do you want?

01:05:31.551 --> 01:05:32.526
I'm like, just send JoJo.

01:05:32.526 --> 01:05:34.760
- But there are people who are
super against that, though.

01:05:34.760 --> 01:05:37.710
- You know, I'm in the middle of this.

01:05:37.710 --> 01:05:39.443
I'm like, I really appreciate giving gifts

01:05:39.443 --> 01:05:40.276
and the whole act of it

01:05:40.276 --> 01:05:41.109
but also I understand that
sometimes you can't give gifts,

01:05:43.206 --> 01:05:45.405
sometimes you don't wanna give gifts,

01:05:45.405 --> 01:05:47.068
sometimes you don't know
the person well enough,

01:05:47.068 --> 01:05:50.284
so you wanna figure it out,
but you wanna say, "Hey,

01:05:50.284 --> 01:05:52.992
"I appreciate you being
a cool friend or whatever

01:05:52.992 --> 01:05:54.871
"but I don't know you very
well but you're, you're cool.

01:05:54.871 --> 01:05:57.527
"So let me buy you
something, I know you want."

01:05:57.527 --> 01:06:00.459
- Yeah now, because I do like
the feeling of giving a gift,

01:06:00.459 --> 01:06:03.876
and I do think about, I
think, every gift I give.

01:06:03.876 --> 01:06:04.709
Which is like, the issue for me is,

01:06:04.709 --> 01:06:05.542
it's a skill that I suck
at, I really, really.

01:06:05.542 --> 01:06:06.375
- Me too.

01:06:10.152 --> 01:06:12.106
- I honestly really suck at it,

01:06:12.106 --> 01:06:16.730
which is why when it comes to
the point, which is Christmas,

01:06:16.730 --> 01:06:17.563
where I have to give gifts,

01:06:17.563 --> 01:06:18.396
I'm just like, I'm shitting myself.

01:06:20.373 --> 01:06:22.429
I'm just like, well me fuck me, man.

01:06:22.429 --> 01:06:26.200
I have to do shopping for other people

01:06:26.200 --> 01:06:27.681
and I suck at shopping for myself.

01:06:27.681 --> 01:06:29.641
And I'm just like, well fuck.

01:06:29.641 --> 01:06:32.979
- One thing I've come to
understand as an adult

01:06:32.979 --> 01:06:33.812
about gift-giving and this is something

01:06:33.812 --> 01:06:34.645
that is an easy trap to fall into,

01:06:36.594 --> 01:06:38.575
if somebody is really into something,

01:06:38.575 --> 01:06:40.400
and they talk about it
a lot though, I do this,

01:06:40.400 --> 01:06:42.712
this is my hobby and stuff,
it's really easy to think,

01:06:42.712 --> 01:06:46.111
oh, I can just buy something
to do with that hobby,

01:06:46.111 --> 01:06:47.621
then that'll work out.

01:06:47.621 --> 01:06:49.076
And that's like a terrible idea

01:06:49.076 --> 01:06:50.411
because if you don't understand the hobby

01:06:50.411 --> 01:06:53.007
as well as they do, you'll
probably not buying something

01:06:53.007 --> 01:06:55.779
that's as useful as you think to them,

01:06:55.779 --> 01:06:56.612
'cause they probably have a vast knowledge

01:06:56.612 --> 01:06:57.445
of the said thing.

01:06:58.757 --> 01:06:59.751
- Yeah and it's also a problem

01:06:59.751 --> 01:07:01.896
when the hobby that they talking about

01:07:01.896 --> 01:07:04.141
is also a collection
that they follow right.

01:07:04.141 --> 01:07:08.035
So every time Aki's birthday
or Christmas rolls around,

01:07:08.035 --> 01:07:10.150
and I'm like, oh, I can just buy her

01:07:10.150 --> 01:07:11.308
something Kingdom Hearts related.

01:07:11.308 --> 01:07:12.141
And then I remember,

01:07:12.141 --> 01:07:14.581
she literally has everything
Kingdom Hearts related.

01:07:14.581 --> 01:07:15.901
So I'm like, what the fuck?

01:07:15.901 --> 01:07:19.268
- It's just like, if you want
to buy something for them

01:07:19.268 --> 01:07:21.434
in that collection, if
they already don't own it

01:07:21.434 --> 01:07:24.345
then that's such a rarity right.

01:07:24.345 --> 01:07:26.230
It's not going to happen,
because they probably...

01:07:26.230 --> 01:07:28.747
If they don't have something
that they don't already own,

01:07:28.747 --> 01:07:29.896
they already know they don't own it.

01:07:29.896 --> 01:07:31.840
And maybe they've already
tried to get it and they can't.

01:07:31.840 --> 01:07:34.758
And if you can get it,
that's a fucking banger gift.

01:07:34.758 --> 01:07:35.884
And that's happened a few times before

01:07:35.884 --> 01:07:37.335
and I'm just like, fuck yeah man,

01:07:37.335 --> 01:07:39.363
I can't wait to give this gift.

01:07:39.363 --> 01:07:41.912
Because you know, sometimes
you just buy a gift

01:07:41.912 --> 01:07:43.686
and you just can't wait to give it, right.

01:07:43.686 --> 01:07:45.166
You're just like...

01:07:45.166 --> 01:07:48.880
And that's what's so
magical about gift-giving,

01:07:48.880 --> 01:07:50.588
but my problem is that,

01:07:50.588 --> 01:07:53.537
it's so rare to find
that one fucking gift,

01:07:53.537 --> 01:07:56.739
that you fucking nail out of the park

01:07:56.739 --> 01:08:00.421
and you're fucking excited
to give it, and it's so hard.

01:08:00.421 --> 01:08:01.254
And that's why 99% of the time, I suck

01:08:01.254 --> 01:08:02.087
and I want to do better.
- What do you do,

01:08:06.676 --> 01:08:07.806
what do you normally to go for?

01:08:07.806 --> 01:08:08.639
- What I normally go for?

01:08:08.639 --> 01:08:10.305
- Yeah.
- Wine.(laughs)

01:08:10.305 --> 01:08:11.537
- What did you get me last year?

01:08:11.537 --> 01:08:12.710
I can't remember what you got on me.

01:08:12.710 --> 01:08:15.858
(calming upbeat music)

01:08:15.858 --> 01:08:18.397
Am I bad friend for not remembering?

01:08:18.397 --> 01:08:20.480
- I mean both of you two..(laughs)

01:08:21.667 --> 01:08:22.657
So it must not have anything that--

01:08:22.657 --> 01:08:23.770
- I remember.

01:08:23.770 --> 01:08:27.485
- I gave you an galleon ten tie thing?*

01:08:27.485 --> 01:08:28.318
It's like the--

01:08:28.318 --> 01:08:30.766
- The tie pin, right?

01:08:30.766 --> 01:08:31.599
- Yeah,

01:08:31.599 --> 01:08:32.432
- Bonginious.

01:08:32.432 --> 01:08:33.265
- I remember giving you that.

01:08:33.265 --> 01:08:35.503
- 'Cause I remember the
last gift I've got you,

01:08:35.503 --> 01:08:36.336
which was the wine
decanter, that was for you.

01:08:36.336 --> 01:08:37.169
(Connor mumbles)

01:08:39.598 --> 01:08:40.431
- Thank you very much.

01:08:40.431 --> 01:08:42.576
- And I remember you got me...

01:08:42.576 --> 01:08:43.450
I mean that was for your birthday,

01:08:43.450 --> 01:08:46.610
and for my birthday, you
got me a cigar-holding case.

01:08:46.610 --> 01:08:47.860
- Yeah the de solidifying Box.

01:08:48.825 --> 01:08:49.658
- I got you a Kurino.

01:08:49.658 --> 01:08:50.491
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

01:08:52.730 --> 01:08:54.060
- What's a Kurino?

01:08:54.060 --> 01:08:56.419
- The Oreimo girl, the figure eight.

01:08:56.419 --> 01:08:57.573
I got him a Kurino figure eight.

01:08:57.573 --> 01:08:59.303
- Because I remember that was
the first gift I gave you guys

01:08:59.303 --> 01:09:00.264
for the first Christmas,

01:09:00.264 --> 01:09:02.387
I which is I remember going
with the JoJo figures.

01:09:02.387 --> 01:09:03.220
- Yeah.
- That's right, yeah

01:09:05.881 --> 01:09:06.714
- It's hard.

01:09:06.714 --> 01:09:07.547
- It's hard.

01:09:07.547 --> 01:09:08.380
- It is hard, 'cause I was like, you know,

01:09:08.380 --> 01:09:09.213
it's like I know Garnt has a
vague interest in this thing.

01:09:12.405 --> 01:09:14.760
I don't think he's too in deep in it

01:09:14.760 --> 01:09:16.285
so I think I can buy something

01:09:16.285 --> 01:09:18.398
to push the hobby a little more.

01:09:18.398 --> 01:09:21.108
- It's scary because as you said,

01:09:21.108 --> 01:09:24.137
if it's something that, you
know they're really into

01:09:24.137 --> 01:09:25.895
and it's like, how are they gonna feel

01:09:25.895 --> 01:09:26.728
if I get them another one?

01:09:26.728 --> 01:09:28.572
- 'Cause I wanna give
them something unique.

01:09:28.572 --> 01:09:29.605
- I wanna give them something

01:09:30.501 --> 01:09:31.819
where it's like, they will look at it

01:09:31.819 --> 01:09:34.054
and go, oh, I remember
when Joey gave me that.

01:09:34.054 --> 01:09:34.967
But that's so hard.

01:09:34.967 --> 01:09:37.021
- I'm jealous of like,

01:09:37.021 --> 01:09:39.117
whenever I see Meilyne gives gifts,

01:09:39.117 --> 01:09:42.929
Meilyne's just like
fucking challenge of rank

01:09:42.929 --> 01:09:44.702
S-tier gift giver, man.

01:09:44.702 --> 01:09:47.277
Like sometimes she gives gifts
to Sydney and I'm just like,

01:09:47.277 --> 01:09:48.110
fuck, why are you going to
do me like this, Meilyne?

01:09:48.110 --> 01:09:48.943
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

01:09:51.789 --> 01:09:54.031
- Meilyne give me a JoJo umbrella,

01:09:54.031 --> 01:09:55.854
that's was pretty good,
I have always wanted one.

01:09:55.854 --> 01:09:57.230
Meilyne knew I wanted one, so she got one.

01:09:57.230 --> 01:09:58.612
- Meilyne, just knows.

01:09:58.612 --> 01:10:00.862
- Meilyne, knows where to get

01:10:02.066 --> 01:10:04.233
all the cool things you
wouldn't normally think about,

01:10:04.233 --> 01:10:06.268
and I'm just like how? Like teach me.

01:10:06.268 --> 01:10:07.101
- Mean while for me I'm
like, I look on Amazon,

01:10:07.101 --> 01:10:07.934
it's not there, I give up.

01:10:09.403 --> 01:10:11.432
- I'm like Meilyne, teach me like.

01:10:11.432 --> 01:10:12.265
- You all need a pool,
what do mean by pool?

01:10:12.265 --> 01:10:13.098
(they all chuckle)

01:10:14.273 --> 01:10:15.323
- A whole pool.

01:10:15.323 --> 01:10:16.156
- Puddle pool?
- Yeah.

01:10:16.156 --> 01:10:16.989
- Yeah definitely.
- Sorry.

01:10:18.204 --> 01:10:20.326
(calming upbeat music)

01:10:20.326 --> 01:10:21.159
- I don't know what I was gonna say.

01:10:21.159 --> 01:10:21.992
- I interrupted you, am sorry.

01:10:21.992 --> 01:10:23.366
(Garnt laughs)

01:10:23.366 --> 01:10:25.320
- The poor escort of "Trash taste".

01:10:25.320 --> 01:10:27.613
- What's the most you've
ever spent on a gift

01:10:27.613 --> 01:10:29.834
or ever received?

01:10:29.834 --> 01:10:31.588
- I got my mom a phone.

01:10:31.588 --> 01:10:32.948
Oh, no plane tickets, I
got her plane tickets.

01:10:32.948 --> 01:10:33.865
- [Garnt] Oh, yeah.

01:10:34.724 --> 01:10:38.391
- I bought my dad like a
$10,000 car engine. (laughs)

01:10:41.960 --> 01:10:44.334
- Oh, my God, Jesus.

01:10:44.334 --> 01:10:48.834
- 'Cause he has this 1960s
beetle, vintage beetle car,

01:10:49.749 --> 01:10:51.039
'cause he loves vintage cars.

01:10:51.039 --> 01:10:51.872
- Yeah I bought Mom a
Ferrari too as well actually.

01:10:51.872 --> 01:10:52.705
(Garnt and Joey laughing)

01:10:54.442 --> 01:10:57.020
- And, and he was like, son...

01:10:57.020 --> 01:10:59.174
Always starts his emails with "son."

01:10:59.174 --> 01:11:02.768
Hello son, may I borrow
some money from you

01:11:02.768 --> 01:11:04.428
to buy this slight engine,

01:11:04.428 --> 01:11:06.214
'cause I'm tryna rebuild this beetle.

01:11:06.214 --> 01:11:09.170
And I realized that was the
moment where I realized,

01:11:09.170 --> 01:11:12.146
I hadn't really given a lot
of gifts to my dad, growing up

01:11:12.146 --> 01:11:12.979
or anything like that.

01:11:12.979 --> 01:11:14.565
And it's always been like small stuff.

01:11:14.565 --> 01:11:16.691
It usually get to that age,

01:11:16.691 --> 01:11:18.931
where you really start to
appreciate your parents,

01:11:18.931 --> 01:11:20.660
especially when you don't
live with them anymore right.

01:11:20.660 --> 01:11:23.567
So I was just like, I'll
just give it to you.

01:11:23.567 --> 01:11:25.364
Just, you don't have to
give me back the money.

01:11:25.364 --> 01:11:27.905
I never seen my dad cry in my life time,

